---
/**
 * ABOUT PAGE — written about the work, not a backstory.
 * No founding year, no "since 20XX", no team photos, no invented owner.
 * Every sentence here must be true, because this is the page an AI engine is
 * most likely to quote.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import TickerBar from '../components/TickerBar.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import SectionHead from '../components/SectionHead.astro';
import WhyUs from '../components/WhyUs.astro';
import CredentialList from '../components/CredentialList.astro';
import TeamGrid from '../components/TeamGrid.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { BRAND, CONTACT, tel, hasStreetAddress } from '../config';
import { KNOWS_ABOUT, coreServices } from '../lib/data';
import { graph, organization, website, webPage, breadcrumbs } from '../lib/schema';

const path = '/about/';
const title = 'About 615 Septic Tank Pumping | Nashville, TN Septic Contractor';
const description =
  'About 615 Septic Tank Pumping — what the company does, the standards the work follows, the Davidson County service area, and how pricing works. Call 24/7.';
const trail = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'About', path },
];
const schema = graph([organization(), website(), webPage({ path, title, description }), breadcrumbs(trail)]);
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path={path} schema={schema}>
  <Breadcrumbs trail={trail} />
  <section class="bg-offwhite py-12 md:py-16">
    <div class="container-site">
      <p class="eyebrow">{CONTACT.serviceArea}</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-[2.4rem] leading-[1.06] text-primary-dark sm:text-5xl">
        About 615 Septic Tank Pumping
      </h1>
      <hr class="rule-accent" />
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-relaxed text-ink">
        {BRAND.name} is a licensed septic tank pumping contractor serving {CONTACT.serviceArea}. The work is residential
        and commercial tank pumping and cleaning, documented inspection, drain field assessment, grease interceptor
        service, and emergency response when a system stops accepting water.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <TickerBar />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-site grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_20rem]">
      <article class="prose-site max-w-none">
        <h2>What the company does</h2>
        <p>
          Septic tank pumping is the core of it. A tank is emptied completely — the floating scum layer and the settled
          sludge on the floor, not just the liquid in between — its inlet and outlet baffles are inspected while it is
          open, its effluent filter is located and rinsed where one is fitted, and the household is left with written
          findings and a dated interval for the next service.
        </p>
        <p>
          Around that sit the services that follow from what a pump-out finds: documented inspection for property
          transactions and insurers, drain field assessment before anyone commits to a five-figure replacement, baffle
          repair, riser installation so a buried access port never has to be dug out again, tank locating on properties
          where nobody knows where it is, and grease interceptor service for commercial kitchens.
        </p>

        <h2>The standards the work follows</h2>
        <p>
          Domestic septage removal in Tennessee is permitted through the Department of Environment and Conservation's
          Division of Water Resources, under Chapter 0400-48-01 of the state rules. Vehicles engaged in septage removal
          must display the firm name and address plus the removal permit number in lettering at least two inches high on
          a contrasting background, along with a department-issued sticker — a check any homeowner can make from their
          own driveway in five seconds, and one worth making.
        </p>
        <p>
          Systems themselves are permitted through the county environmental health office. Davidson County is one of
          Tennessee's contract counties, which can mean an additional county permit alongside the state process, and
          reviews here are stricter than the state average because Middle Tennessee is karst country — soluble limestone
          with a thin soil mantle and solution features that route water underground with very little filtration.
        </p>

        <h2>How pricing works</h2>
        <p>
          Published ranges appear on this site because the first question is always what it costs. A standard
          residential pump-out runs $275 to $525 in Tennessee according to published pricing, and reported Davidson
          County jobs span $199 to $796 depending on tank size and access. Those are third-party figures, cited on the
          pages where they appear.
        </p>
        <p>
          A price for a specific property is confirmed before any work starts. Anything that needs excavating, fitting
          or replacing is quoted first — nothing is done on the assumption that a homeowner standing next to an open
          tank will agree to it.
        </p>

        <h2>Service area</h2>
        <p>
          {CONTACT.serviceAreaLong}. That covers Bellevue, Antioch, Hermitage, Donelson and Madison as primary areas;
          Green Hills, Goodlettsville, Old Hickory and Joelton; and the smaller communities where septic is the only
          option — Whites Creek, Bells Bend, Forest Hills, Oak Hill, Una and Pasquo. Each area page sets out the ground
          conditions and failure patterns specific to that part of the county.
        </p>

        <h2>What is not claimed on this site</h2>
        <p>
          There are no customer reviews, star ratings, testimonials, award badges or job counts anywhere on this site,
          because there is no verified stock of them to publish. Fabricated reviews carry FTC penalties of up to
          $53,088 per violation, and beyond the legal question, a review that was written by the company is not
          evidence of anything.
        </p>
        <p>
          What this site offers instead is checkable: published cost ranges with their sources linked, the specific
          methods and standards the work follows, a cost estimator that shows its formula, and technical detail precise
          enough that a reader can judge whether the person who wrote it knows the trade. Genuine reviews will be
          published here as they are received, through the
          <a href="/leave-a-review/"> review page</a>, and not before.
        </p>
      </article>

      <aside class="lg:sticky lg:top-28 lg:self-start">
        <div class="card p-5">
          <p class="font-display text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary-dark">Contact</p>
          <hr class="rule-accent" />
          <address class="mt-4 not-italic leading-relaxed">
            <p class="font-semibold text-primary-dark">{BRAND.name}</p>
            {
              hasStreetAddress ? (
                <p class="text-ink-soft">
                  {CONTACT.address.street}<br />
                  {CONTACT.address.locality}, {CONTACT.address.region} {CONTACT.address.postalCode}
                </p>
              ) : (
                <p class="text-ink-soft">{CONTACT.address.locality}, {CONTACT.address.region}</p>
              )
            }
            <p class="mt-3">
              <a href={tel} class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-primary-dark">{CONTACT.phoneDisplay}</a>
            </p>
            <p><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`} class="underline">{CONTACT.email}</a></p>
          </address>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">{CONTACT.hoursHuman}</p>
          <a href={tel} class="btn btn-accent mt-4 w-full" data-cta="about-call">
            <Icon name="phone" size={20} /> Call now
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="card mt-6 p-5">
          <p class="font-display text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary-dark">Areas of expertise</p>
          <hr class="rule-accent" />
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-[0.98rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            {KNOWS_ABOUT.map((k) => (
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <Icon name="check" size={16} class="mt-1 shrink-0 text-primary-light" />
                <span>{k}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
          <div class="mt-5 border-t border-line pt-4">
            <CredentialList />
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container-site">
      <SectionHead eyebrow="How the work is done" heading="Four things that are true of every visit" />
      <div class="mt-10"><WhyUs headingLevel={3} /></div>
      <div class="mt-12"><TeamGrid /></div>
      <p class="mt-10">
        <a href="/services-menu/" class="btn btn-outline">All {coreServices.length} core services →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    heading={`Call ${CONTACT.phoneDisplay}`}
    body={`${BRAND.name} covers ${CONTACT.serviceArea}. A person answers and takes the details.`}
    secondaryLabel="Send property details"
  />
</Base>
